[Nuzlocke\Block pause-menu Retry and Quit]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=Retry, Restart and Quit in the pause menu do nothing, so an event can't be abandoned to save a life, and Retry on the results screens acts as Continue, so a just-wrecked car can't be raced again. Resume and Continue still work.
// Pause handler 1 (around 00190800): selected item -1 = Retry (confirm "$PRRetryRace"), -2 = Quit
// ("$QUIT"). The two branches to those confirm dialogs become nops, so both fall through to the exit.
patch=1,EE,0019088C,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,0019089C,word,00000000
// Pause handler 2 (around 001910DC): jump table 004B7D70, indexed by item + 1. Quit (001911F8),
// Retry (00191110), Restart junction (00191230) and Retry (00191268) now go to the exit at 00191580.
patch=1,EE,004B7D70,word,00191580
patch=1,EE,004B7D78,word,00191580
patch=1,EE,004B7D84,word,00191580
patch=1,EE,004B7D88,word,00191580
// Results screens: Retry now does what Continue does, so a just-wrecked car can't be raced again.
// (V1.1 made Retry do nothing instead, which left the screen locked: its exit path sets a busy flag
// that only a real action clears, so Continue then froze.)
// Race results handler (0019AD98, near "finalizeRaceResults"): command 8 (Retry) runs command 7's code
// (0019AED8, which advances the results). s0 is set back to the screen object in the delay slot.
patch=1,EE,0019ADC4,word,10000044
patch=1,EE,0019ADC8,word,0080802D
// End-of-event handler 00191B58: item 1 (Retry) goes to item 0's path at 00191C38, with v0 = 01F60000
// as that path expects.
patch=1,EE,00191CC0,word,1000FFDD
patch=1,EE,00191CC4,word,3C0201F6
// End-of-event handler 00191FA8: item 1 (Retry) goes to the item 0 / -2 path at 001921A0, with
// v1 = 004F0000 as that path expects.
patch=1,EE,0019206C,word,1000004C
patch=1,EE,00192070,word,3C03004F

