[Nuzlocke\Mode\Limited Selection]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=Before every event the tracker picks 2 of your usable cars for Race events and 2 for Crash junctions; every other healthy car is [BENCHED] until the next event. No car is picked twice in a row. Needs nuzlocke.exe V2.
// Tells the tracker the mode is on.
patch=1,EE,000FE130,word,00000001

[Nuzlocke\Mode\Revive tokens]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=Win streaks earn revive tokens that give a wrecked car one life back: every 3 wins in a row on Easy (hold up to 3), 5 on Medium (hold 2), 8 on Hard (hold 1). A held token also saves a run that would otherwise end. Needs nuzlocke.exe V2.
// Tells the tracker the mode is on.
patch=1,EE,000FE134,word,00000001

[Nuzlocke\Mode\Event Roulette]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=After every event the tracker picks the next one at random from every World Tour event (ones you haven't won yet first), and every other event is locked on the map until you've played it. A reroll for every 5 wins (hold up to 3). Every rank is open; your rank, results and cars are untouched. Needs nuzlocke.exe V2.
// Tells the tracker the mode is on.
patch=1,EE,000FE138,word,00000001
// The unlock check (part 4 of Block dead cars in garage) then opens only the tracker's pick, or every
// event when nothing is picked.
// Every rank tab on the map open: the tab is locked when your rank is below it (001A362C slt v0,v0,s2).
patch=1,EE,001A362C,word,0000102D

[Nuzlocke\Mode\Event Roulette - Unlock all cars]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=Every car is unlocked from the start, so a rank 10 event never has to be raced with starter cars (made for Event Roulette, works on its own too). Each car joins the run with full lives the first time it shows up in the garage. Needs nuzlocke.exe V2.
// The game's car checks answer as if its debug "all cars" byte (profile +0x402) were set, without
// setting it: each lbu of that byte becomes "load 1".
// Car unlocked (00133FB0) and its second flag (00134008):
patch=1,EE,00133FC0,word,24020001
patch=1,EE,00134018,word,24020001
// Number of cars the garage lists: all 80 instead of the unlocked count (+0x3FC):
patch=1,EE,001BB930,word,24030001
patch=1,EE,002B101C,word,24020001

[Nuzlocke\Harder AI\Easy]
author=Nuzlocke mod
description=Harder opponents, Easy level: faster and more aggressive. Enable only one Harder AI level. Corners at 0.8625 of the racing line's limit (0.9125 on aggressive stretches); far from the player, 1.5-4.5 s per section quicker than their pace schedule; catch-up from 40 m behind the player (up to +18 m/s); ease-off from 50 m ahead of the player (to 0.91 x the player's speed); speed cap 97 m/s. Opponents go for takedowns more often, from further away and sooner after the start, block you for longer and slam 15% harder. See docs/research/ai-catchup.md and ai-aggression.md.
// Corner speed factor (game: 0.8, aggressive 0.85)
patch=1,EE,0029EE1C,word,3C013F5C
patch=1,EE,0029EE20,word,3421CCCD
patch=1,EE,0029EE30,word,3C013F69
patch=1,EE,0029EE34,word,3421999A
// Far-mode pace: offset to each section's planned time, clamped to -4.5..-1.5 s (game: -4..+4)
patch=1,EE,0029A138,word,3C01C090
patch=1,EE,0029A298,word,3C01C090
patch=1,EE,0029A154,word,3C01BFC0
patch=1,EE,0029A2B4,word,3C01BFC0
// Speed cap ceiling 88 -> 97 m/s (217 mph), loaded as a constant instead of tuning value 01C913F4.
// Far from the player (two copies): lui at,cap / mtc1 at,f3 / min speed via lwc1 f1,0x13F8(v0) / clamp.
patch=1,EE,0029A190,word,3C0142C2
patch=1,EE,0029A198,word,44811800
patch=1,EE,0029A19C,word,C44113F8
patch=1,EE,0029A1A0,word,46010028
patch=1,EE,0029A1A4,word,46030029
patch=1,EE,0029A2F0,word,3C0142C2
patch=1,EE,0029A2F8,word,44811800
patch=1,EE,0029A2FC,word,C44113F8
patch=1,EE,0029A300,word,46010028
patch=1,EE,0029A304,word,46030029
// Near the player (flat cap): lui at,cap / sw at,0xA44(s0) in the branch delay slot.
patch=1,EE,0029ABE0,word,3C0142C2
patch=1,EE,0029ABE8,word,AE010A44
// Catch-up: the brain update's call to the target-speed function (00298FEC) goes through a wrapper at
// 000FFA00. When this opponent is more than 40 m behind the player (track progress), boost =
// min(0.225 x (gap - 40), 18) m/s: its target speed becomes at least the player's speed + boost, and
// its top speed (car+0x1354, mph) is set to stock + boost. Otherwise top speed is reset to stock.
// When it is more than 50 m AHEAD of the player, its target speed is held to 0.91 x the player's speed
// (but at least 40 m/s), so a leader can be caught.
patch=1,EE,00298FEC,word,0C03FE80
patch=1,EE,000FFA00,word,27BDFFC0
